  "discussion": "A north-northwest swell and a smaller overlapping west-northwest swell will slowly decline today, keeping tiny surf for north and west shores through much of the week. A small northwest swell may arrive Thursday, followed by a slightly larger north- northwest swell this weekend. The current south swell will continue a slow decline today. South shore surf will drop below seasonal average and will remain relatively small through much of the week. A moderate south- southwest swell is expected this weekend, bringing surf heights up to or perhaps slightly above seasonal averages. Rough trade wind swell will produce east shore surf just above seasonal average through Tuesday, then decline later in the week as trade winds decrease.",
